                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237967511",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198013845646",
                            "num_reviews": 27,
                            "playtime_forever": 127,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 127,
                            "last_played": 1770846718
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "You play as Sarah, and explore her weird dreamscapes. This is a nice, short, vibey platformer, probably inspired by games like Yume Nikki, but doesn't have as much disturbing weirdness. That's not to say the disturbing stuff is nonexistent. Mostly, it's just a series of weird places and weird characters. Very delightful at times, in fact. Sometimes not.\n\nThis is, basically, an item collection game - no fighting, and while you can die to hazards you just pop back to the start of the screen. Many items give you abilities - an umbrella lets you glide through air, and such - and lets you progress to different areas. Nothing mindblowing, but I thought it was fun and pretty creative. The pixel art style is pretty great, and music is very moody.\n\nIt's not a long game. Walkthrough estimates say this game is about 1 hour - I took about 4 because I like to explore. And I had to restart the game, because I'm pretty sure I ran into a progress-breaking bug, but since the game is pretty short, I didn't mind that much.\n\nI liked the vibes, most of all. I'm definitely a dream mood vibe kinda person, so I'm rating it 4/5. Might be 3 for regular short collectathon platform enthusiasts and 2.5 for random achievement enthusiasts.",
